    },
    "thm-riesz-representation-for-hilbert-space": {
      "id": "thm-riesz-representation-for-hilbert-space",
      "path": "items/thm-riesz-representation-for-hilbert-space.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "exact_statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let $H$ be a real or complex Hilbert space and let $f$ be a bounded linear functional on $H$ ([[def-dual-space-of-a-normed-space]]). Then there is a unique $y\\in H$ with\n\n$$f(x)=\\langle x,y\\rangle\\qquad\\text{for every }x\\in H,$$\n\nand $\\|f\\|=\\|y\\|$, where $\\|f\\|$ is the dual norm ([[def-operator-norm]]). Under the first-variable-linear convention the representing vector depends conjugate-linearly and isometrically on $f$: if $f_i$ is represented by $y_i$ and $a,b$ are scalars, then $af_1+bf_2$ is represented by $\\overline a\\,y_1+\\overline b\\,y_2$.",
      "sha256": "0655811a363020d7b0df4d6ebbbc7ebb437adb0f4e098b7fb96959d3dc98c7c1",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
