    "thm-fourier-basis-and-parseval-on-the-n-torus": {
      "id": "thm-fourier-basis-and-parseval-on-the-n-torus",
      "path": "items/thm-fourier-basis-and-parseval-on-the-n-torus.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "exact_statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $n\\ge1$\nand let $e_k(x)=\\exp(2\\pi i\\,k\\cdot x)$, $k\\in\\mathbb Z^n$, be the coordinate\ncharacters on $\\mathbb T^n$\n([[def-the-one-dimensional-torus-and-normalized-haar-integral]],\n[[def-fourier-coefficients-and-trigonometric-polynomials]]). Then:\n\n1. $(e_k)_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^n}$ is an orthonormal family in the complex Hilbert\n   space $L^2(\\mathbb T^n)$;\n2. it is an orthonormal basis: its closed linear span is $L^2(\\mathbb T^n)$;\n3. consequently the Fourier expansion\n   $f=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^n}\\widehat f(k)e_k$ and Parseval's identity\n   $$\\|f\\|_2^2=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^n}|\\widehat f(k)|^2,\\qquad \\langle f,g\\rangle=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^n}\\widehat f(k)\\overline{\\widehat g(k)}$$\n   hold for all $f,g\\in L^2(\\mathbb T^n)$, in the finite-subset-net sense; and\n4. the Fourier coefficient map is a surjective linear isometry of\n   $L^2(\\mathbb T^n)$ onto $\\ell^2(\\mathbb Z^n,\\mathbb C)$.\n\nNo Hilbert tensor-product identification is used anywhere.",
      "sha256": "6d017415a6b810647e7c94b874eeaf15f46699e548ad6957fc16aad60600d968",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
      "consumers": [
        "def-fd-periodic-solenoidal-spaces",
        "def-fd-bounded-solenoidal-spaces"
      ],
      "home_kind": "canonical-root-item",
      "original_page_homes": [
        {
          "path": "library/functional-analysis/orthonormal-bases-parseval-and-fourier-series.md",
          "page": "orthonormal-bases-parseval-and-fourier-series",
          "is_B": false,
          "status": "published"
        }
