    "lem-zero-extension-from-w-one-p-zero": {
      "id": "lem-zero-extension-from-w-one-p-zero",
      "path": "items/lem-zero-extension-from-w-one-p-zero.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "exact_statement": "Assume Countable Choice. For any open $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$,\n$n\\ge1$, any $1\\le p\\le\\infty$ and any\n$\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}$, extension by zero\n$$E_0u(x)=u(x)\\ \\ (x\\in\\Omega),\\qquad E_0u(x)=0\\ \\ (x\\notin\\Omega),$$\nacted on representatives, sends $W_0^{1,p}(\\Omega;\\mathbb K)$ linearly into\n$W^{1,p}(\\mathbb R^n;\\mathbb K)$. For every $u\\in W_0^{1,p}(\\Omega;\\mathbb K)$\nand every coordinate direction $i$, the class $D_i(E_0u)$ is the zero\nextension of the class $D_iu$, and every $L^p$ component norm is preserved:\n$$\\|E_0u\\|_{L^p(\\mathbb R^n)}=\\|u\\|_{L^p(\\Omega)},\\qquad \\|D_i(E_0u)\\|_{L^p(\\mathbb R^n)}=\\|D_iu\\|_{L^p(\\Omega)},$$\nso that $\\|E_0u\\|_{W^{1,p}(\\mathbb R^n)}=\\|u\\|_{W^{1,p}(\\Omega)}$.",
      "sha256": "3d7e19a22d44a255088e19059ae137c708aef4f124ad24b5072d3918e8391a2f",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
      "consumers": [
        "def-fd-bounded-solenoidal-spaces"
      ],
      "home_kind": "canonical-root-item",
      "original_page_homes": [
